# 5. Beacon Current Release & Product Context

## Current Quarter · Committed

### Simplified Workspace Navigation

**Status:** In progress  
**Target:** November release

Includes:

- simplified top-level navigation;
- preservation of current eligible views;
- preservation of user defaults where supported;
- clearer distinction between personal and discoverable views.

Does not include:

- unrestricted user-created layouts;
- dynamic AI-generated recommendations;
- new specialty-wide access rules.

---

### Preference Migration

**Status:** In progress

Existing supported preferences will migrate where technically safe.

Auto-enrolling every user into new specialty views is not part of the current commitment.

---

### Permission-Aware Content Rendering

**Status:** In progress

A user may discover a page or view without automatically receiving access to every restricted component inside it.

Access remains governed by the underlying authorization model.

---

## Planned · Not Yet Committed

### Expanded Custom Views

Users may eventually have more control over creating and organizing their own views.

This is not part of the current release.

### Broader Recommendation Logic

Future releases may evaluate more contextual approaches to deciding which views appear in personalized areas.

Current behavior remains rules-based.

### Reusable Clinical Component Library Expansion

Additional reusable UI and workflow components are planned for future quarters.

---

## Common Expectation Gaps

### "For You means AI recommendations"

Not established.

The current recommendation model is rule-based.

### "Everyone in a specialty gets the same views automatically"

Not established.

Eligibility and access remain separate concepts.

### "Users can fully customize their workspace"

Not part of the current release.

### "A design mock means the feature has been approved"

False.

Design exploration does not establish product decision status.

